WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.790
Earlier this week the Council held its monthly meeting for November.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:17.040
It started with a presentation from Sam Huo, who was representing the ownership of Pegasus Golf Club.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.200
He updated the Council about Pegasus hosting  
the NZPGA Championship tournament for the

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.740
next three years, and talked about future
plans to construct accommodation and conference

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.620
facilities at the golf course.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.140
The Council also formally adopted the Kaiapoi
Town Centre Plan: 2028 and Beyond.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.559
It promotes a vision of a vibrant Town Centre
that embraces the river, attracts visitors

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:44.710
and new businesses and creates enjoyable public
spaces.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.140
For the first time, it also includes Masterplans
for the Mixed-Use Business Areas that were

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.129
set aside following the Canterbury earthquakes.

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:56.280
Because of the large amount of land available
for development, it’s considered a long-term

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.360
plan and could take the next 20 to 30 years to be fully realised.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.380
The Council also approved a submission on
behalf of the Waimakariri District to the

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.260
Draft Regional Public Transport Plan.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.500
This document plans for the region’s public
transport needs for the next 10 years and

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.930
beyond.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:19.450
Our council strongly advocated for higher
frequency services between Christchurch and

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.189
our main towns.

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:26.090
We also asked that the committee be more ambitious
in trialling new transport technologies and

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:31.400
developing demand responsive services for
our smaller or more remote population centres.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.900
The final monthly Council Meeting for the
year, will be held on Tuesday 4 December.

